%S A400900 0,1,1,4,12,68,556,8149,214885,10472494,945332511,158347971394,
%T A400900 49332562510545,28672533385601677,31192967779020021980,
%U A400900 63733129035373037158274,245358865044150520252667893,1785238944295982092117987867659,24619922720328650756209120653084155,645231335249993229308288016267949176029
%N A400900 Number of connected simple unlabeled bipartite Eulerian graphs on 2*n vertices that admit an automorphism interchanging the two parts of the bipartition.
%C A400900 The two parts of the bipartition are the red and blue vertex sets in a proper vertex coloring: every edge joins vertices of different colors.
%C A400900 The required automorphism interchanges these two sets.
%F A400900 a(n) = Sum_{k|n, k odd} mu(k)/k * [x^(2*n/k)] (log E(x) - (1/2)*log B(x^2)), for n >= 1, where
%F A400900 E(x) = 1 + Sum_{m>=1} x^(2*m) * Sum_{lambda partition of m} 2^(H(lambda)-l(lambda)+epsilon(lambda))/z_lambda.
%F A400900 H(lambda) = Sum_i ceiling(lambda_i/2) + Sum_{i<j} gcd(lambda_i,lambda_j).
%F A400900 epsilon(lambda) = 1 if all parts of lambda are even, and 0 otherwise.
%F A400900 B(x) = (1+x)/(1-x) + Sum_{p,q>=1} x^(p+q) * Sum_{alpha partition of p, beta partition of q} 2^(G(alpha,beta)-l(alpha)-l(beta)+kappa(alpha,beta))/(z_alpha*z_beta).
%F A400900 G(alpha,beta) = Sum_i Sum_j gcd(alpha_i,beta_j).
%F A400900 For any partition rho, l(rho) is its number of parts and z_rho = Product_{j>=1} (j^m_j(rho) * m_j(rho)!), where m_j(rho) is the number of parts equal to j.
%F A400900 Let u = min_i nu_2(alpha_i) and v = min_j nu_2(beta_j).
%F A400900 Then kappa(alpha,beta) = 1 if u = v; kappa(alpha,beta) = #{i: nu_2(alpha_i) < v} if u < v; and kappa(alpha,beta) = #{j: nu_2(beta_j) < u} if u > v.
%F A400900 Here nu_2(t) is the exponent of 2 in t, mu is the Moebius function, and [x^r] denotes coefficient extraction.
%e A400900 For n = 3, the only graph counted is the cycle C_6: a rotation by one vertex interchanges its red and blue vertex sets.
%e A400900 The other connected bipartite Eulerian graph on 6 vertices, K_{2,4}, is not counted because its two parts have different sizes. Thus a(3) = 1.
%Y A400900 Cf. A243320, A400899.
%K A400900 nonn,new
%O A400900 1,4
